WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.787
The fit interview: a weak answer, and a strong one.

2
00:00:03.887 --> 00:00:05.886
"Tell me about a time you led a team."

3
00:00:06.136 --> 00:00:07.502
Here is a weak answer.

4
00:00:07.522 --> 00:00:15.414
"We had a group project and it was quite hard, but we worked well together and got a good mark."

5
00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:18.548
Vague, all "we", no numbers, and no lesson.

6
00:00:18.798 --> 00:00:24.286
Now a strong one, using STAR-L: situation, task, action, result, learning.

7
00:00:24.386 --> 00:00:28.959
"Our five-person team was two weeks behind on a client report."

8
00:00:28.979 --> 00:00:31.527
"I was asked to get it back on track."

9
00:00:31.547 --> 00:00:39.039
"I split the work into daily goals, took the analysis no one wanted, and ran a 10-minute check-in each morning."

10
00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:43.325
"We delivered two days early, and the client extended the project."

11
00:00:43.345 --> 00:00:48.004
"I learned to make progress visible early, so problems surface fast."

12
00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:55.682
Specific, first person, a number, and a lesson. Build 6 to 8 stories like this once, and reuse them.
